// Test simfile with hand-worked note times and notes per second, for calibrating ddr-trainer's
// chart analyzer (src/chart_analyzer.rs), whose tests check the values below. Generated by
// test_resources/make_test_simfiles.py, so edit that instead of this.
//
// The BPM changes and stops, which all the charts share:
//   beat   0    8    16   25
//   BPM    120  240  180  120     (0.5, 0.25, 1/3 and 0.5 s per beat)
//   stops  0.75 s on beat 2, and 0.5 s on beat 5 1/3 (written as 5.333)
// A note on a stop's beat is hit as the stop starts, so the stop only delays later notes.
// Times are seconds from beat 0.
//
// Notes per second come from a 1 s window starting at each note, holding the notes from it up
// to (but not including) 1 s later. The statistics are the mean, median and max of how many
// notes each window holds, so the last notes in a chart, with less after them, count fewer.
//
//   chart      mean            median  max
//   Beginner   0               0       0    nothing in it
//   Easy       24/13 = 1.846   2       3    times across BPM changes and stops
//   Medium     1               1       1    one note
//   Hard       81/16 = 5.0625  6       6    8th notes at 180 BPM (1/6 s apart), half jumps
//   Challenge  98/23 = 4.261   4       8    quarter, 8th and 16th notes at 120 BPM
//
// Easy's notes, their times, and how many notes each one's window holds:
//   beat    0  1    2  3     4     5 1/3   6     8     9    10    12    16    17
//   time    0  0.5  1  2.25  2.75  3.4167  4.25  5.25  5.5  5.75  6.25  7.25  7.5833
//   window  2  2    1  2     2     2       1     3     3    2     1     2     1
// It also has a row with only a hold end (beat 11) and one with only a mine (beat 14), which
// aren't notes.
// Hard's windows each hold 6 notes, except the last five (5, 4, 3, 2, 1). Its notes are 1/6 s
// apart, which an f64 can't hold exactly, so the note 6 later can come out a hair under 1 s
// after one, and has to be left out of its window all the same.
// Challenge's windows, by measure: 2 2 2 3 | 4 4 4 4 4 5 6 7 | 8 8 7 6 5 5 4 3 2 2 | 1
//
// Of the same windows: the mode (ties go to the smaller), the standard deviation, and the min,
// which only takes the windows that end by the last note (0 with none):
//   chart      mode  std            min
//   Easy       2     sqrt(74)/13    1
//   Medium     1     0              0
//   Hard       6     sqrt(655)/16   6
//   Challenge  4     sqrt(2080)/23  2
// Both stops are between Easy's first and last notes: 2 stops, 1.25 s, 15/91 of its 7.5833 s.
// The other charts start after them.
//
// Seconds from each note to the next, the fastest 2, 3, 5, 7 and 15 notes in a row (in notes per
// second: a note fewer than the run has, over its seconds) and the closest two jumps (1 over
// their seconds):
//   chart      mean    median  mode   max   fastest 2  3  5  7    15   jumps
//   Easy       91/144  0.5     0.5    1.25          4  4  2  1.8  0    0
//   Hard       1/6     1/6     1/6    1/6           6  6  6  6    6    3
//   Challenge  3/11    0.25    0.125  0.5           8  8  8  8    5.6  2
// Easy's gaps: 0.5 0.5 1.25 0.5 2/3 5/6 1 0.25 0.25 0.5 1 1/3. Its fastest 5 notes take 2 s
// (from 5.25 s) and its fastest 7 take 10/3 s (from 4.25 s).
// Challenge's gaps: 0.5 four times, 0.25 eight, 0.125 eight, 0.5 twice. The mode's tie goes to
// 0.125. Its fastest 15 notes take 2.5 s: six gaps of 0.25, then the eight of 0.125.
//
// The most notes in any 5, 10 and 30 s (each over its seconds), and the longest run of notes
// with no gap over 1 s:
//   chart      5 s  10 s  30 s  run
//   Easy       9    13    13    10 notes, 16/3 s (2.25 to 7.5833: the 1.25 s gap before breaks it)
//   Medium     1    1     1     1 note, 0 s
//   Hard       16   16    16    16 notes, 2.5 s
// Easy's best 5 s start at 2.75 s.
#TITLE:NPS Stats;
#ARTIST:ddr-trainer;
#MUSIC:nps_stats.ogg;
#OFFSET:0.000000;
#BPMS:0.000=120.000,8.000=240.000,16.000=180.000,25.000=120.000;
#STOPS:2.000=0.750,5.333=0.500;

//---------------dance-single - nothing in it----------------
#NOTES:
     dance-single:
     nothing in it:
     Beginner:
     1:
     0.412,0.356,0.250,0.100,0.000:
// measure 0: empty
0000
0000
0000
0000
,  // measure 1: empty
0000
0000
0000
0000
;

